extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 26: Dinosaur Swamp printed 62-64 (cache p063-p065, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the OCR and checked line by line against renders of printed 62 and 63. Heading and lore on printed 62, the stat block, special skills, equipment and Homespun Armor on 63, the weapons, vehicle, money and cybernetics at the top of 64. || GROUP: under the section heading Barbarians (printed 59-69), which states no group of its own; its guidelines (printed 61) call the region''s barbarians Wilderness Scouts in effect, and the entry calls the Wild Knives part Wilderness Scout. The entry states no S.D.C. base, only +4D6+10 to base physical S.D.C., the same shape as the Dinosaur Hunter, so men_of_arms is false (the core 1D6 S.D.C.) and occ_group is optional, matching the held Wilderness Scout. || XP: the fourth column of the Experience Point Tables, printed 74 (cache p075), which the table heads Wild Knives Barbarian and shares with the Swamp Stomper and Naturalist; read off a 300 dpi render, every low bound is the previous high plus one. || P.P.E.: Base P.P.E. 2D6+8, which does not increase with experience; stored as ppe_base 2d6+8 with no per-level phrase. || BONUSES: printed as Special Bonus. +4D6+10 S.D.C., +1D4 P.E., +2 to save vs poisons and disease (toxins_poisons 2, disease 2), and +1 vs Horror Factor at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 14 (six at_level entries, none at level 1). || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Lore: Dinosaurs, Lore: Swamp & Everglades and Track Dinosaurs are this book''s special skills, shipped in ~246; Track Dinosaurs takes the +15% printed beside Track Animals, which the list says includes dinosaurs. Cooking is Cook; Horsemanship (General) is Horsemanship: General; Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals; Speak Native Language at 90% is Language: Native Tongue. W.P.: Knife plus two Ancient and two Modern of choice; the catalog does not separate ancient from modern. || RELATED: count 6 with no floor; the schedule is one each at levels 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15. Medical prints +10% beside First Aid and +5% beside Holistic Medicine, so it is three entries. Pilot: Motor & Sail Boat is read as Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil and Boat: Sail Type, Kayak/Canoes as Boat: Paddle Types/Canoe/Kayak, all +10%; Hovercycle as Hovercycles, Skycycles & Rocket Bikes with no bonus. Technical is any except Cyberjacking with +10% to Gemology, Language, Lore, Breed Dogs and Rope Works, so two entries that do not overlap; the other high-tech skills it also bars are named in the note only, because the book does not list them. Exotic Animals and Holistic Medicine counting as two selections is in the note, not enforced. || HAND TO HAND: Expert; Martial Arts (or Assassin if evil) costs one related skill. || MONEY: the book prints 2D4x1000 in trade goods and nothing else. Trade goods are not coin, so starting_money is not stored; the figure is a restriction line. || EQUIPMENT: Homespun Armor is granted as the held dinosaur-swamp-homespun-armor row (shipped in ~248). Not stored as rows: a belt with pouches or detachable purses and 1D4 waterproof sacks; modern optics are coveted but the character starts with none. They are in GM Notes."
