# Wild Knives Warrior

## Lore

The Wild Knives are the warriors of the eastern barbarian tribes: part fighter, part raider, part hunter and part Wilderness Scout. They live off the land by fishing and by hunting animals and dinosaurs, and by raiding outsiders, rival tribes, Mutant Barbarians, D-Bees and even supernatural beings before melting back into the forest or swamp. The Minions of Splugorth and Horune Pirates, who carry off humans and D-Bees for arenas and slave markets, are hated above all and struck down wherever they are found. Rivals, by contrast, are prey to be plundered again and again, and are usually left alive with their homes and crops intact.

The tribes are mostly human nomads roaming a territory they claim as their own. When resources run short the Wild Knives are sent out to raid, and young bands go into rival lands for game, revenge or the fight itself; a warrior''s worth is measured by the enemies he has earned. Death in battle for the good of the tribe is a noble end. The wilderness itself is both provider and rival, and only those willing to risk life and limb every day survive it.

## GM Notes

Lore: Dinosaurs (the same skill as the Swamp Stomper''s and Dinosaur Hunter''s) covers living dinosaurs and the creatures of Dinosaur Swamp. Lore: Swamp & Everglades covers the swamplands'' ecology, hazards, wildlife, waterways and routes. Track Dinosaurs is part of the Track Animals skill for this class, as useful for avoiding dinosaurs as for finding them.

Homespun Armor: piecemeal non-environmental armor of dinosaur hide and bone or salvaged M.D.C. scraps; see the gear row for its M.D.C., penalties and cost.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: a belt with pouches or detachable purses and 1D4 waterproof sacks. Binoculars, gun scopes, nightvision goggles and other high-tech optics are prized, but the character starts with none.

Weapons: one for every W.P. with 1D4 E-Clips (or 200 rounds) each where they apply. Wild Knives love Vibro-Blades and start with one Vibro-Knife; they also covet long-range energy weapons and magic items but start with none.

Most barbarian tribes number 50 to 500 members; the largest reach 1,000 to 2,000.
